SYSTEM WORKFLOW:
----------------

1. User accesses the application via web browser
2. User logs in with credentials (or browses public pages)
3. System validates credentials and assigns appropriate role
4. Based on role, user sees relevant dashboard:
   - ADMIN: Full access to all management features
   - STUDENT: Access to personal records and academic info
5. User performs operations (CRUD):
   - Create: Add new records (admissions, users, etc.)
   - Read: View existing data (grades, attendance, etc.)
   - Update: Modify records (profile, enrollment, etc.)
   - Delete: Remove records (with proper authorization)
6. All operations are validated and logged
7. Changes are reflected in real-time across the system
8. User logs out when session is complete

DATABASE DESIGN:
----------------

Main Tables:

1. users
   - id (Primary Key)
   - username
   - email
   - password_hash
   - role (Admin/Student/Professor)
   - created_at
   - updated_at

2. students
   - id (Primary Key)
   - user_id (Foreign Key)
   - first_name
   - last_name
   - dob
   - gender
   - address
   - phone
   - guardian_name
   - guardian_phone
   - batch_id

3. admissions
   - id (Primary Key)
   - student_id (Foreign Key)
   - applied_course
   - application_date
   - status (Pending/Approved/Rejected)
   - documents_submitted

4. courses
   - id (Primary Key)
   - course_code
   - course_name
   - credits
   - department
   - semester

5. enrollments
   - id (Primary Key)
   - student_id (Foreign Key)
   - course_id (Foreign Key)
   - enrollment_date
   - status (Active/Completed/Dropped)

6. attendance
   - id (Primary Key)
   - student_id (Foreign Key)
   - course_id (Foreign Key)
   - date
   - status (Present/Absent/Late)
   - marked_by

7. assignments
   - id (Primary Key)
   - course_id (Foreign Key)
   - title
   - description
   - due_date
   - file_path
   - created_by

8. exams
   - id (Primary Key)
   - course_id (Foreign Key)
   - exam_type (Midterm/Final/Quiz)
   - exam_date
   - total_marks

9. exam_results
   - id (Primary Key)
   - exam_id (Foreign Key)
   - student_id (Foreign Key)
   - marks_obtained
   - grade

10. fees
    - id (Primary Key)
    - student_id (Foreign Key)
    - fee_type
    - amount
    - due_date
    - status (Paid/Unpaid)

11. payments
    - id (Primary Key)
    - fee_id (Foreign Key)
    - amount
    - payment_date
    - payment_method
    - transaction_id

12. events
    - id (Primary Key)
    - title
    - description
    - event_date
    - venue
    - created_by

